      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Here are three sealed jars of colourless gas. One holds pure oxygen, one holds pure carbon dioxide, and one holds ordinary air. They look exactly the same, so looking won't tell you which is which. But chemists sort every sample into a few kinds, and the sorting doesn't depend on how it looks. It depends on the particles inside. So let's zoom in, and see how particles tell an element, a compound and a mixture apart.",
