      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Start with the first split. A substance is one particular kind of matter, with its own kind of particle. In jar A, every particle is identical: two oxygen atoms joined together. Jar B is the same idea. Every particle is one carbon atom joined to two oxygen atoms. A sample that contains only one substance is called a pure substance. Now look at the air. There are different kinds of particle here: mostly nitrogen, some oxygen, a little argon and carbon dioxide, all moving around separately. A sample with two or more substances mixed together is a mixture.",
