      "pronunciationText": "Pure substances split again. Oxygen is an element. An element is a substance made of only one kind of atom. Here, each particle happens to be a molecule, two atoms joined together, but both atoms are oxygen. So a molecule doesn't make something a compound. Iron is an element too. In a piece of iron, every atom is an iron atom. Elements are the substances listed in the periodic table, and an element's formula has just one symbol.",
