      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "A mixture is different. Its substances are just mingled, so each one keeps its own particles and its own properties. Here are iron filings stirred into yellow sulfur powder. The iron and the sulfur aren't bonded to each other, so a magnet can pull the iron straight out. And there's no fixed recipe. You could mix in a pinch of sulfur or a whole spoonful, and it's still a mixture of iron and sulfur. Proportions that can change are called variable composition, and that's a mark of a mixture.",
