      "requestAttempts": 1,
      "pronunciationText": "Mixtures split once more, by how evenly they're mixed. Stir salt into water until it disappears. The salt breaks up into its ions, and they spread evenly between the water molecules. Every drop has the same composition, and you can't see separate parts. That's a homogeneous mixture, the same all the way through. Air is one too. Now look at the iron and sulfur again. There are grey patches and yellow patches, and a scoop from one side isn't the same as a scoop from the other. That's a heterogeneous mixture. Its composition differs from region to region.",
